course: dictionary
lesson: 11685
title: Attached: fixed, fond, or sent along
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The clues around it tell you which meaning to use. «The label was attached to my bag with a string.» The label was joined to the bag, so attached means fixed or joined to something.
explain: «Please see the attached photo.» Here the clues are please see and photo, and you usually find these in an email. Attached means sent along with the message. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check: «Please see the photo sent along» still makes sense, so this meaning fits.
explain: «Ruby became attached to her puppy as soon as she held it.» Now the clues are about feelings. Ruby did not join herself to the puppy with a string. Attached means fond of and loving someone or something.
fact: Attached is the past form of the verb attach. The other forms are attach, attaches and attaching.
fact: «Attached» can mean joined or fixed to something, like a badge on a jacket.
fact: «Attached» can mean fond of and loving someone or something, like a friend or a pet.
fact: «Attached» can mean sent along with an email or letter, as in «please see attached».
fact: The phrase «strings attached» means there are hidden conditions or rules you must agree to before you get something.
exercise: «The name tag was attached to his coat.» What does attached mean here? | Sent along in an email | Torn into pieces | Fond of his coat | *Fixed or joined to something
exercise: «Please see the attached form for the trip.» Where would you most likely find the attached form? | Hidden in the library | Inside the school bag | Under the desk | *In an email or letter sent with the message
exercise: «Lily was very attached to her old teddy bear.» What does attached mean here? | *Fond of and loving | Broken and thrown away | Sent along with a letter | Joined to the bear with a string
test: «The free ticket has strings attached: you must bring a parent.» What does strings attached mean? | The ticket is made of real string | It is a magic ticket | *There are hidden conditions or rules to follow | The ticket is free for everyone with no rules
test: «Yesterday Sam attached a note to the door.» Which form of the verb attach is attached here? | *Past form | Plural form | Question form | Future form
exam: «The puppy was attached to its owner, so it followed her everywhere.» Which meaning of attached is used? | *Fond of and loving someone | Tied with a string | Sent along with an email | Joined or fixed to something
